<<tag character:Narrator>>
<<tag lore_id:lore_anastasia_rocker_journal>>
Narrator: Tucked between the cushion and the arm of the rocking chair is a small leather journal, the page bookmarked with a pressed leaf.
Narrator: The handwriting is careful, schoolroom-neat, dated forty-two years ago.
Narrator: "Today the girl came out of the mud again. She has not aged. I had thought I dreamed her the first time."
Narrator: "Her name is Lirael. She said it without moving her mouth. She said it inside my chest."
Narrator: "I am going to learn the song. I am going to learn it for her."
Narrator: A child's drawing is folded inside the back cover — two figures holding hands, one shining.
===
